## Wait for Compute Nodes

Continue after the compute nodes boot and complete their install. A node is
ready when `systemd` has finished starting it; `degraded` counts too, since
an image often carries a unit that fails harmlessly. To check one node:

```bash
ssh ${compute_prefix}1 systemctl is-system-running
```

The recipe waits for every node, for up to `node_boot_timeout` seconds. A node
that is not ready by then has failed to provision; check its console. A node
that still carries `/run/ohpc-preprovision` is still running the system it had
before the reset, and is not counted.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Optional fixed wait before checking the compute nodes -->
<!-- ohpc_command sleep "${provision_wait:-0}" -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Wait for the compute nodes to finish booting -->
<!-- ohpc_command deadline=$(( SECONDS + ${node_boot_timeout:-1800} )) -->
<!-- ohpc_command until pdsh -S -w "${compute_prefix}[1-${num_computes}]" \ -->
<!-- ohpc_command         "test ! -e /run/ohpc-preprovision && timeout 60 systemctl is-system-running --wait \ -->
<!-- ohpc_command         | grep -qxE 'running|degraded'" >/dev/null 2>&1; do -->
<!-- ohpc_command     if (( SECONDS >= deadline )); then -->
<!-- ohpc_command         echo "compute nodes: FAILED, not booted in ${node_boot_timeout:-1800}s; check the node consoles" -->
<!-- ohpc_command         exit 1 -->
<!-- ohpc_command     fi -->
<!-- ohpc_command     echo "Waiting for compute nodes..." -->
<!-- ohpc_command     sleep 10 -->
<!-- ohpc_command done -->
<!-- ohpc_command echo "compute nodes: OK" -->
<!-- ohpc_end -->
